#!/usr/bin/env perl

use strict;
use warnings;

# Grab --pt-config before Mojolicious sees the argv, then pass the rest through.
use Getopt::Long qw(:config pass_through);
GetOptions( 'pt-config=s' => \( my $pt_config ) );
$ENV{NISABA_CONFIG} = $pt_config if defined $pt_config;

use Mojolicious::Commands;
Mojolicious::Commands->start_app('App::Nisaba::WebSSO');

=head1 NAME

mojo_nisaba_sso - OpenID Connect SSO provider for App::Nisaba

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  # Development server (port 3000)
  mojo_nisaba_sso daemon

  # Custom port
  mojo_nisaba_sso daemon -l http://*:8082

  # Production (prefork)
  mojo_nisaba_sso prefork -l https://*:443

  # With a custom nisaba config
  mojo_nisaba_sso daemon --pt-config /etc/nisabarc

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Starts the App::Nisaba OpenID Connect SSO provider. This application
implements the OIDC Authorization Code flow with PKCE support, providing
a login/consent UI backed by LDAP user accounts.

Standard OIDC endpoints:

    /.well-known/openid-configuration   Discovery
    /authorize                          Authorization endpoint
    /token                              Token endpoint
    /userinfo                           UserInfo endpoint

All standard Mojolicious server commands (C<daemon>, C<prefork>, etc.)
are supported after any C<--pt-config> argument.

=head1 ENVIRONMENT

=head2 NISABA_CONFIG

Path to the nisabarc config file. Overridden by C<--pt-config>.

=head2 NISABA_SECRET

Session secret. Set this to a long random string in production.

=head1 CONFIG KEYS (nisabarc)

In addition to the standard App::Nisaba LDAP settings, the following
keys are used by the SSO provider:

=head2 oidcbase

LDAP base DN for OIDC client entries (oidcRelyingParty). Required
for the SSO provider to start.

=head2 ssoIssuer

The issuer identifier for this OpenID Provider. This should be the
base URL of the SSO provider (e.g. C<https://sso.example.com>).
Defaults to the request URL origin if not set.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<App::Nisaba>, L<App::Nisaba::WebSSO>

=cut
